      "line": 216,
      "evidence": "The driver extracts and imports review_verifiers.py from the caller-supplied --base commit, after only checking that --base is an ancestor of HEAD. It rejects changes to the verifier in the current fix diff, but does not establish that the verifier at --base predates the PR or comes from a trusted target branch. A PR can therefore modify the verifier in an earlier commit, then run this self-review with that weakened verifier as its grading authority.",
      "remediation": "Load verifiers from a trusted target/base SHA outside the PR, or fail closed unless the verifier path is proven unchanged from that trusted SHA across the whole PR range; do not treat the immediately preceding fix commit as trusted merely because it is an ancestor.",
